  "summary": {
    "as": "Introduced in House",
    "asOf": "2025-04-02",
    "date": "2026-11-12T20:42:24Z",
    "text": "Renewable Natural Gas Incentive Act of 2025\n\nThis bill establishes a federal tax credit, through 2035, equal to $1 for each gallon of renewable natural gas (compressed or liquified gas derived from biomass)\u00a0or gasoline gallon equivalent of a nonliquid renewable natural gas\u00a0used or sold for use as a fuel in a motor vehicle, a motorboat, or in aviation. Under the bill, a gasoline gallon equivalent\u00a0of a nonliquid renewable natural gas\u00a0is the amount of the fuel that has a Btu content of 124,800 (higher heating value). Specific registration and other conditions apply."
  },
